<title>SPAIN: Spain July C/A deficit 8.6 bln pesetas.</title>
<headline>Spain July C/A deficit 8.6 bln pesetas.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain gave the following figures (in billions of pesetas):</p>
<p> BALANCE OF PAYMENTS		  JULY 96    JUNE 96   JULY 95</p>
<p>  C/A balance			     -8.6	-30.8     -41.6</p>
<p>  Trade balance			 -163.5     -152.4    -182.3</p>
<p>  Services				 334.4	230.0     256.5</p>
<p>  Net tourism receipts		 364.5	247.0     306.4</p>
<p>  Other services			 -30.1	-17.0     -49.9</p>
<p>  Dividend income		     -169.7     -137.5    -116.0</p>
<p>  Transfers				 -9.8	 29.0	 0.2</p>
<p>  CAPITAL ACCOUNT			104.2	145.6     113.6</p>
<p>  FINANCIAL ACCOUNT		   -107.9	 19.5     -28.2</p>
<p>  Spanish investment abroad	  -91.4	  3.9     -41.7</p>
<p>  Foreign investment in Spain	 34.2	245.7     427.5</p>
<p>  Spanish loans,deposits abroad   -416.1	102.9    -602.4</p>
<p>  Foreign loans, deps in Spain     506.3     -284.7     214.2</p>
<p>  Movement of reserves		-141.0	-48.3     -25.8</p>
<p>NOTE: The Bank of Spain said latest figures were provisional. Non-classified element (errors and omissions) in latest capital account figures is positive 12.3 billion pesetas. The financial account category was introduced in January 1996.</p>
</text>
